857
01:00:19.739 --> 01:00:22.059
Gary Young: Aasimar is good.

858
01:00:22.859 --> 01:00:23.179
Gary Young: Yes.

859
01:00:23.339 --> 01:00:23.819
David Mendenhall[?]: That's right.

860
01:00:24.699 --> 01:00:25.579
Gary Young: Or celestial.

861
01:00:25.739 --> 01:00:25.899
Gary Young: Sorry.

862
01:00:29.819 --> 01:00:32.379
Gary Young: That would be something she hasn't seen much of.

863
01:00:32.699 --> 01:00:37.739
Gary Young: And, you know, it's close to a connection to the sun.

864
01:00:38.059 --> 01:00:38.219
Gary Young: Yeah.

865
01:00:39.419 --> 01:00:40.619
Gary Young: Sunlight does he appear.

866
01:00:41.179 --> 01:00:41.419
Gary Young [?]: Okay.

867
01:00:41.579 --> 01:00:42.139
Gary Young [?]: That's good.

868
01:00:42.299 --> 01:00:42.539
Gary Young: All right.

869
01:00:42.699 --> 01:00:43.579
Gary Young: Is she shiny?

870
01:00:44.379 --> 01:00:49.980
David Mendenhall: Anyway, I was going to say Brewbarry is the only patron who ever gave me a 10 out of 10 on the survey.

871
01:00:53.099 --> 01:00:53.819
Gary Young: I think he did.

872
01:00:53.980 --> 01:00:54.379
Gary Young: Yes.

873
01:00:57.899 --> 01:00:58.299
Kostadis Roussos: All right.

